%% Proposed system context. The outer box is a product boundary, not one trusted process.
%% Internal browser/server/worker trust zones are expanded in component.mmd.
flowchart LR
  accTitle: System context — proposed browser-game platform
  accDescr: The author and optional external model provider surround a proposed product boundary. Browser authoring and local play, the independently validating platform service, generation worker and managed infrastructure are internal components. Provider output and worker candidates remain untrusted until the publication gate approves data.
    author["Author<br/>Writer, teacher or small-team member"]
    provider["External model provider<br/>Optional; outside product boundary"]

    subgraph product["Proposed browser-game platform — overall product boundary"]
        client["Browser client<br/>Authoring and trusted 2D runtime<br/>Gameplay state stays local"]
        api["Platform service<br/>Projects, versions and job status<br/>Independent validation and publication gate"]
        ai["Generation service<br/>Intent, candidate data and bounded repair<br/>Output remains untrusted at platform gate"]
        storage[("Managed infrastructure<br/>Project/job records and events<br/>Private approved artifacts")]
        client -->|"Story, parameters and status requests"| api
        api -->|"Status, safe errors; ready game and simplifications"| client
        api -->|"Generation request with version IDs"| ai
        ai -->|"Worker-checked candidate or failure"| api
        api <-->|"Persist / retrieve records and approved artifacts"| storage
    end

    author -->|"Story, settings and local gameplay"| client
    client -->|"Progress, game, ending or safe error"| author
    ai -->|"Minimum required story context"| provider
    provider -->|"Untrusted model output"| ai

    classDef external fill:#fff1eb,stroke:#9a492d,color:#3f261e;
    classDef gate fill:#e6f2ed,stroke:#33745b,color:#17382b;
    class provider external;
    class api gate;
